From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:46:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vrend: offer an eight bit stencil format that needs no depth
 plane

vrend had no image format of stencil alone as a depth-stencil target: the
table named VIRGL_FORMAT_X24S8_UINT, the stencil view of a packed image,
and no VIRGL_FORMAT_S8_UINT, so a guest that wanted a stencil buffer and no
depth was handed a depth-stencil image with a depth plane it never used. A
32-bit float depth beside the stencil is eight bytes per texel where one
would do, and Android's hardware renderer asks for stencil and no depth for
every window it draws.

The table now has VIRGL_FORMAT_S8_UINT, stored as GL_STENCIL_INDEX8. The
format probe attached every format with stencil to the depth-stencil
attachment point, where a texture without a depth plane is incomplete, so
the probe would have found the new format unusable as a target and left it
without VIRGL_BIND_DEPTH_STENCIL; the target path binds a stencil-only
image at the stencil attachment point, and the probe now does too.

An image with one plane must also take the other plane off the framebuffer.
The depth-only path already detached the stencil attachment; the stencil-only
path left the depth attachment of whatever image the framebuffer held before.
A stencil-only image that followed a depth-stencil one, a window's depth-stencil
buffer and then a renderbuffer of stencil alone, was paired with that image's
depth plane: GL_FRAMEBUFFER_UNSUPPORTED on the host, and every draw after the
switch was lost. The stencil-only path now detaches the depth attachment.

A guest's GL_STENCIL_INDEX8 renderbuffers and textures choose the new format
as soon as the capset names it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vrend/vrend_formats.c  |  6 +++++-
 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c b/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
index d1db8bb999cb4de5f608869adb6eec26dc455b12..0f5e6c2eb0767d655ec6b76326646a282eaf5688 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_formats.c
@@ -91,6 +91,7 @@ static struct vrend_format_table base_depth_formats[] =
     /* this is probably a separate format */
     { VIRGL_FORMAT_Z32_FLOAT_S8X24_UINT, GL_DEPTH32F_STENCIL8, GL_DEPTH_STENCIL, GL_FLOAT_32_UNSIGNED_INT_24_8_REV, NO_SWIZZLE, view_class_unsupported },
     { VIRGL_FORMAT_X24S8_UINT, GL_STENCIL_INDEX8, GL_STENCIL_INDEX, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, NO_SWIZZLE, view_class_unsupported },
+    { VIRGL_FORMAT_S8_UINT, GL_STENCIL_INDEX8, GL_STENCIL_INDEX, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, NO_SWIZZLE, view_class_unsupported },
   };
 
 static struct vrend_format_table gl_z32_format[] = {
@@ -478,8 +479,11 @@ static void vrend_add_formats(struct vrend_format_table *table, int num_entries)
       const struct util_format_description *desc = util_format_description(table[i].format);
       GLenum attachment;
 
+      /* The attachment point vrend_fb_bind_texture_id() will use: a texture
+       * with no depth is incomplete behind a depth attachment. */
       if (util_format_has_stencil(desc))
-        attachment = GL_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT;
+        attachment = util_format_has_depth(desc) ? GL_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT
+                                                 : GL_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT;
       else
         attachment = GL_DEPTH_ATTACHMENT;
       glFramebufferTexture2D(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, attachment, GL_TEXTURE_2D, tex_id, 0);
diff --git a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
index 20af151e94d97a840bf70cb3e0be0f4148af1031..4c12d45e31d84cc7aa4c15c702c0ab905a949263 100644
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -3163,15 +3163,22 @@ void vrend_fb_bind_texture_id(struct vrend_resource *res,
       break;
    }
 
-   if (attachment == GL_DEPTH_ATTACHMENT) {
+   /* An image with a single plane leaves the other attachment point alone, so
+    * the framebuffer keeps what an earlier image put there: a stencil-only
+    * image that follows a depth-stencil one would be paired with that image's
+    * depth plane, a combination the host cannot draw to. Detach the plane the
+    * image does not have. */
+   if (attachment == GL_DEPTH_ATTACHMENT || attachment == GL_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT) {
+      const GLenum other = attachment == GL_DEPTH_ATTACHMENT ?
+                           GL_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT : GL_DEPTH_ATTACHMENT;
       switch (res->target) {
       case GL_TEXTURE_1D:
-         glFramebufferTexture1D(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, GL_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT,
+         glFramebufferTexture1D(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, other,
                                 GL_TEXTURE_1D, 0, 0);
          break;
       case GL_TEXTURE_2D:
       default:
-         glFramebufferTexture2D(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, GL_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT,
+         glFramebufferTexture2D(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, other,
                                 GL_TEXTURE_2D, 0, 0);
          break;
       }
